!  Atomic and Plasma-Material Interaction Data for Fusion (Supplement
!  to the journal Nuclear Fusion) 8 (1998).
!
! All of these data were downloaded from the CFADC web site.
! The only differences are that the H+ + H2 elastic scattering
! data required additional interpolation to fill in missing energy
! values and that the D + D+ (classical) charge exchange cross 
! section was extrapolated to higher energies by rescaling the
! analytic form of the Janev-Smith cross section.
!
!  The treatment of elastic scattering in a Monte Carlo neutral transport
!  code can be made more efficient by replacing scatterings with deviations
!  smaller than some minimum cutoff angle by an effective scattering at
!  that minimum angle. The total cross section is computed so as to keep
!  the diffusion cross section at its expected value (the viscosity cross
!  section is modified only very slightly). So, data are included here
!  for both no cutoff (for comparison purposes) and a cutoff of 5 degrees.
!
!  A separate set of data provides the scattering angles broken up into
!  bins of equal probability. These data are also used in the Monte Carlo
!  calculation.
!
$ ELS H [+0] (G) H [+1] (G) H [+0] (G) H [+1] (G)
& XST CUTOFF_00 #ELSPLINE 
!
!  This is a cubic spline fit to the total elastic scattering cross 
!  section with no cutoff. A linear extrapolation (in log space) is
!  is defined at the ends of the energy range.
!
